[{"id":"saala-38-86-2","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pitam vas","en":"I ask you (all)"},{"bs":"pita vas","en":"he/it asks you (all)"},{"bs":"i pitajte!","en":"and (you all) ask!"},{"bs":"bivate pitani","en":"you (all) are asked"}],"ref":"38:86","answerWord":"أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ","answerSound":"audio/dbe1acc5713b012b6913.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say (O Muhammad, unto mankind): I ask of you no fee for this, and I am no simulating.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["قُلْ","مَآ","أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ","عَلَيْهِ","مِنْ","أَجْرٍ","وَمَآ","أَنَا۠","مِنَ","ٱلْمُتَكَلِّفِينَ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-2-189-0","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pitaju te","en":"they ask you"},{"bs":"i pitajte!","en":"and (you all) ask!"},{"bs":"pitao si ih","en":"you asked them"},{"bs":"pa pitaj!","en":"so ask!"}],"ref":"2:189","answerWord":"يَسْـَٔلُونَكَ","answerSound":"audio/7f8f7ba5909bc01beaaa.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They ask thee, (O Muhammad), of new moons, say: They are fixed seasons for mankind and for the pilgrimage. It is not righteousness that ye go to houses by the backs thereof (as do the idolaters at certain seasons), but the righteous man is he who wardeth off (evil). So go to houses by the gates thereof, and observe your duty to Allah, that ye may be successful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["يَسْـَٔلُونَكَ","عَنِ","ٱلْأَهِلَّةِ","قُلْ","هِىَ","مَوَٰقِيتُ","لِلنَّاسِ","وَٱلْحَجِّ","وَلَيْسَ","ٱلْبِرُّ","بِأَن","تَأْتُوا۟","ٱلْبُيُوتَ","مِن","ظُهُورِهَا","وَلَٰكِنَّ","ٱلْبِرَّ","مَنِ","ٱتَّقَىٰ","وَأْتُوا۟","ٱلْبُيُوتَ","مِنْ","أَبْوَٰبِهَا","وَٱتَّقُوا۟","ٱللَّهَ","لَعَلَّكُمْ","تُفْلِحُونَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-2-219-14","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"i pitaju te","en":"and they ask you"},{"bs":"pita vas","en":"he/it asks you (all)"},{"bs":"sigurno ćemo ih pitati","en":"We will surely ask them"},{"bs":"pitan je","en":"he/it was asked"}],"ref":"2:219","answerWord":"وَيَسْـَٔلُونَكَ","answerSound":"audio/42b4609088127a0b657a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They question thee about strong drink and games of chance. Say: In both is great sin, and (some) utility for men; but the sin of them is greater than their usefulness. And they ask thee what they ought to spend. Say: that which is superfluous. Thus Allah maketh plain to you (His) revelations, that haply ye may reflect.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["يَسْـَٔلُونَكَ","عَنِ","ٱلْخَمْرِ","وَٱلْمَيْسِرِ","قُلْ","فِيهِمَآ","إِثْمٌ","كَبِيرٌ","وَمَنَٰفِعُ","لِلنَّاسِ","وَإِثْمُهُمَآ","أَكْبَرُ","مِن","نَّفْعِهِمَا","وَيَسْـَٔلُونَكَ","مَاذَا","يُنفِقُونَ","قُلِ","ٱلْعَفْوَ","كَذَٰلِكَ","يُبَيِّنُ","ٱللَّهُ","لَكُمُ","ٱلْءَايَٰتِ","لَعَلَّكُمْ","تَتَفَكَّرُونَ"],"marked":[14],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-29-61-1","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pitao si ih","en":"you asked them"},{"bs":"biva pitan","en":"he/it is asked"},{"bs":"pita vas","en":"he/it asks you (all)"},{"bs":"pa ga pitaj!","en":"so ask him!"}],"ref":"29:61","answerWord":"سَأَلْتَهُم","answerSound":"audio/53846aebf3feb4268c8a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And if thou wert to ask them: Who created the heavens and the earth, and constrained the sun and the moon (to their appointed work)? they would say: Allah. How then are they turned away?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["وَلَئِن","سَأَلْتَهُم","مَّنْ","خَلَقَ","ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ","وَٱلْأَرْضَ","وَسَخَّرَ","ٱلشَّمْسَ","وَٱلْقَمَرَ","لَيَقُولُنَّ","ٱللَّهُ","فَأَنَّىٰ","يُؤْفَكُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-2-134-11","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"bivate pitani","en":"you (all) are asked"},{"bs":"pitali ste ga","en":"you (all) asked it"},{"bs":"pitaj!","en":"ask!"},{"bs":"i neka upitaju","en":"and let them ask"}],"ref":"2:134","answerWord":"تُسْـَٔلُونَ","answerSound":"audio/70e2705e485516f71118.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Those are a people who have passed away. Theirs is that which they earned, and yours is that which ye earn. And ye will not be asked of what they used to do.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["تِلْكَ","أُمَّةٌ","قَدْ","خَلَتْ","لَهَا","مَا","كَسَبَتْ","وَلَكُم","مَّا","كَسَبْتُمْ","وَلَا","تُسْـَٔلُونَ","عَمَّا","كَانُوا۟","يَعْمَلُونَ"],"marked":[11],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-51-12-0","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pitaju","en":"they ask"},{"bs":"pitali ste","en":"you (all) asked"},{"bs":"upitana je","en":"she/it was asked"},{"bs":"pitani su","en":"they were asked"}],"ref":"51:12","answerWord":"يَسْـَٔلُونَ","answerSound":"audio/5061ad1758302d23d577.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They ask: When is the Day of Judgment?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["يَسْـَٔلُونَ","أَيَّانَ","يَوْمُ","ٱلدِّينِ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-21-23-1","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"biva pitan","en":"he/it is asked"},{"bs":"i pitajte!","en":"and (you all) ask!"},{"bs":"pitali ste ih","en":"you (all) asked them"},{"bs":"pita ga","en":"he/it asks him"}],"ref":"21:23","answerWord":"يُسْـَٔلُ","answerSound":"audio/015b8668787a4357fb10.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He will not be questioned as to that which He doeth, but they will be questioned.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["لَا","يُسْـَٔلُ","عَمَّا","يَفْعَلُ","وَهُمْ","يُسْـَٔلُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-4-32-17","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"i pitajte!","en":"and (you all) ask!"},{"bs":"i bivaju pitani","en":"and they are asked"},{"bs":"pa zaista ćemo pitati","en":"so surely we will ask"},{"bs":"i zaista ćete biti pitani","en":"and surely you (all) will be asked"}],"ref":"4:32","answerWord":"وَسْـَٔلُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/7cc93ae95dee001b5ead.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And covet not the thing in which Allah hath made some of you excel others. Unto men a fortune from that which they have earned, and unto women a fortune from that which they have earned. (Envy not one another) but ask Allah of His bounty. Lo! Allah is ever Knower of all things.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["وَلَا","تَتَمَنَّوْا۟","مَا","فَضَّلَ","ٱللَّهُ","بِهِۦ","بَعْضَكُمْ","عَلَىٰ","بَعْضٍ","لِّلرِّجَالِ","نَصِيبٌ","مِّمَّا","ٱكْتَسَبُوا۟","وَلِلنِّسَآءِ","نَصِيبٌ","مِّمَّا","ٱكْتَسَبْنَ","وَسْـَٔلُوا۟","ٱللَّهَ","مِن","فَضْلِهِۦٓ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","كَانَ","بِكُلِّ","شَىْءٍ","عَلِيمًا"],"marked":[17],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-10-72-3","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pitao sam vas","en":"I asked you (all)"},{"bs":"pita ga","en":"he/it asks him"},{"bs":"biva pitan","en":"he/it is asked"},{"bs":"pa pitaj!","en":"so ask!"}],"ref":"10:72","answerWord":"سَأَلْتُكُم","answerSound":"audio/1924b40d8f06689a115e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"But if ye are averse I have asked of you no wage. My wage is the concern of Allah only, and I am commanded to be of those who surrender (unto Him).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["فَإِن","تَوَلَّيْتُمْ","فَمَا","سَأَلْتُكُم","مِّنْ","أَجْرٍ","إِنْ","أَجْرِىَ","إِلَّا","عَلَى","ٱللَّهِ","وَأُمِرْتُ","أَنْ","أَكُونَ","مِنَ","ٱلْمُسْلِمِينَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-10-94-7","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa pitaj!","en":"so ask!"},{"bs":"pita te","en":"he/it asks you"},{"bs":"bivamo pitani","en":"we are asked"},{"bs":"pitao sam vas","en":"I asked you (all)"}],"ref":"10:94","answerWord":"فَسْـَٔلِ","answerSound":"audio/0e5c67e95d292bc3889a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And if thou (Muhammad) art in doubt concerning that which We reveal unto thee, then question those who read the Scripture (that was) before thee. Verily the Truth from thy Lord hath come unto thee. So be not thou of the waverers.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["فَإِن","كُنتَ","فِى","شَكٍّ","مِّمَّآ","أَنزَلْنَآ","إِلَيْكَ","فَسْـَٔلِ","ٱلَّذِينَ","يَقْرَءُونَ","ٱلْكِتَٰبَ","مِن","قَبْلِكَ","لَقَدْ","جَآءَكَ","ٱلْحَقُّ","مِن","رَّبِّكَ","فَلَا","تَكُونَنَّ","مِنَ","ٱلْمُمْتَرِينَ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-16-43-8","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa pitajte!","en":"so (you all) ask!"},{"bs":"pitao si ih","en":"you asked them"},{"bs":"biva pitan","en":"he/it is asked"},{"bs":"pitaju","en":"they ask"}],"ref":"16:43","answerWord":"فَسْـَٔلُوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/07fec1cbeb42d480085b.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And We sent not (as Our messengers) before thee other than men whom We inspired - Ask the followers of the Remembrance if ye know not! -","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["وَمَآ","أَرْسَلْنَا","مِن","قَبْلِكَ","إِلَّا","رِجَالًا","نُّوحِىٓ","إِلَيْهِمْ","فَسْـَٔلُوٓا۟","أَهْلَ","ٱلذِّكْرِ","إِن","كُنتُمْ","لَا","تَعْلَمُونَ"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-16-56-8","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"zaista ćete biti pitani","en":"surely you (all) will be asked"},{"bs":"i pitaj ih!","en":"and ask them!"},{"bs":"pita te","en":"he/it asks you"},{"bs":"bivaju pitani","en":"they are asked"}],"ref":"16:56","answerWord":"لَتُسْـَٔلُنَّ","answerSound":"audio/15214b9ea289cdaf5255.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And they assign a portion of that which We have given them unto what they know not. By Allah! but ye will indeed be asked concerning (all) that ye used to invent.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["وَيَجْعَلُونَ","لِمَا","لَا","يَعْلَمُونَ","نَصِيبًا","مِّمَّا","رَزَقْنَٰهُمْ","تَٱللَّهِ","لَتُسْـَٔلُنَّ","عَمَّا","كُنتُمْ","تَفْتَرُونَ"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-17-101-6","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa pitaj!","en":"so ask!"},{"bs":"pitaj ih!","en":"ask them!"},{"bs":"pa ih pitajte!","en":"so (you all) ask them!"},{"bs":"i bivaju pitani","en":"and they are asked"}],"ref":"17:101","answerWord":"فَسْـَٔلْ","answerSound":"audio/b200cdc821c40f35f3c4.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And verily We gave unto Moses nine tokens, clear proofs (of Allah's Sovereignty). Do but ask the Children of Israel how he came unto them, then Pharaoh said unto him: Lo! I deem thee one bewitched, O Moses.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["وَلَقَدْ","ءَاتَيْنَا","مُوسَىٰ","تِسْعَ","ءَايَٰتٍۭ","بَيِّنَٰتٍ","فَسْـَٔلْ","بَنِىٓ","إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ","إِذْ","جَآءَهُمْ","فَقَالَ","لَهُۥ","فِرْعَوْنُ","إِنِّى","لَأَظُنُّكَ","يَٰمُوسَىٰ","مَسْحُورًا"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-70-10-1","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pita","en":"he/it asks"},{"bs":"i zaista će biti pitani","en":"and surely they will be asked"},{"bs":"pita te","en":"he/it asks you"},{"bs":"pitam vas","en":"I ask you (all)"}],"ref":"70:10","answerWord":"يَسْـَٔلُ","answerSound":"audio/fbbfa8ddc91b858bec02.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And no familiar friend will ask a question of his friend","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["وَلَا","يَسْـَٔلُ","حَمِيمٌ","حَمِيمًا"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-2-108-6","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pitan je","en":"he/it was asked"},{"bs":"pitali ste ih","en":"you (all) asked them"},{"bs":"pa zaista ćemo pitati","en":"so surely we will ask"},{"bs":"bivate pitani","en":"you (all) are asked"}],"ref":"2:108","answerWord":"سُئِلَ","answerSound":"audio/967a727ff46ac6b98f92.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Or would ye question your messenger as Moses was questioned aforetime? He who chooseth disbelief instead of faith, verily he hath gone astray from a plain road.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["أَمْ","تُرِيدُونَ","أَن","تَسْـَٔلُوا۟","رَسُولَكُمْ","كَمَا","سُئِلَ","مُوسَىٰ","مِن","قَبْلُ","وَمَن","يَتَبَدَّلِ","ٱلْكُفْرَ","بِٱلْإِيمَٰنِ","فَقَدْ","ضَلَّ","سَوَآءَ","ٱلسَّبِيلِ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-2-186-1","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pitao te je","en":"he/it asked you"},{"bs":"pita","en":"he/it asks"},{"bs":"pitali ste ga","en":"you (all) asked it"},{"bs":"pitani su","en":"they were asked"}],"ref":"2:186","answerWord":"سَأَلَكَ","answerSound":"audio/8cbb66474240dddbf6d0.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And when My servants question thee concerning Me, then surely I am nigh. I answer the prayer of the suppliant when he crieth unto Me. So let them hear My call and let them trust in Me, in order that they may be led aright.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["وَإِذَا","سَأَلَكَ","عِبَادِى","عَنِّى","فَإِنِّى","قَرِيبٌ","أُجِيبُ","دَعْوَةَ","ٱلدَّاعِ","إِذَا","دَعَانِ","فَلْيَسْتَجِيبُوا۟","لِى","وَلْيُؤْمِنُوا۟","بِى","لَعَلَّهُمْ","يَرْشُدُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-2-211-0","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pitaj!","en":"ask!"},{"bs":"bivate pitani","en":"you (all) are asked"},{"bs":"pitali su","en":"they asked"},{"bs":"pitaju te","en":"they ask you"}],"ref":"2:211","answerWord":"سَلْ","answerSound":"audio/8b52af8c822ac94016ad.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Ask of the Children of Israel how many a clear revelation We gave them! He who altereth the grace of Allah after it hath come unto him (for him), lo! Allah is severe in punishment.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["سَلْ","بَنِىٓ","إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ","كَمْ","ءَاتَيْنَٰهُم","مِّنْ","ءَايَةٍۭ","بَيِّنَةٍ","وَمَن","يُبَدِّلْ","نِعْمَةَ","ٱللَّهِ","مِنۢ","بَعْدِ","مَا","جَآءَتْهُ","فَإِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","شَدِيدُ","ٱلْعِقَابِ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-5-102-1","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pitao ih je","en":"he/it asked them"},{"bs":"pitaj!","en":"ask!"},{"bs":"da upita","en":"so that he/it may ask"},{"bs":"bivamo pitani","en":"we are asked"}],"ref":"5:102","answerWord":"سَأَلَهَا","answerSound":"audio/c2d0daa3f1f040fdedb7.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"A folk before you asked (for such disclosures) and then disbelieved therein.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["قَدْ","سَأَلَهَا","قَوْمٌ","مِّن","قَبْلِكُمْ","ثُمَّ","أَصْبَحُوا۟","بِهَا","كَٰفِرِينَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-7-6-0","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa zaista ćemo pitati","en":"so surely we will ask"},{"bs":"pitaju","en":"they ask"},{"bs":"pitao sam vas","en":"I asked you (all)"},{"bs":"zaista ćete biti pitani","en":"surely you (all) will be asked"}],"ref":"7:6","answerWord":"فَلَنَسْـَٔلَنَّ","answerSound":"audio/c8f249c04d7cc28de499.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then verily We shall question those unto whom (Our message) hath been sent, and verily We shall question the messengers.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["فَلَنَسْـَٔلَنَّ","ٱلَّذِينَ","أُرْسِلَ","إِلَيْهِمْ","وَلَنَسْـَٔلَنَّ","ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"saala-7-6-4","words":["verb:saala"],"options":[{"bs":"i zaista ćemo pitati","en":"and surely we will ask"},{"bs":"i pitajte!","en":"and (you all) ask!"},{"bs":"pitali ste","en":"you (all) asked"},{"bs":"pitao sam te","en":"I asked you"}],"ref":"7:6","answerWord":"وَلَنَسْـَٔلَنَّ","answerSound":"audio/26daf8cb1763f3596e1d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then verily We shall question those unto whom (Our message) hath been sent, and verily We shall question the messengers.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pitati","en":"to ask"},"passage":["فَلَنَسْـَٔلَنَّ","ٱلَّذِينَ","أُرْسِلَ","إِلَيْهِمْ","وَلَنَسْـَٔلَنَّ","ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"سَأَلَ"}},{"id":"istajala-51-14-6","words":["verb:istajala"],"options":[{"bs":"požurujete","en":"you (all) hasten"},{"bs":"požurivali ste","en":"you (all) hastened"},{"bs":"požuruje","en":"he/it hastens"},{"bs":"požuruju me","en":"they ask me to hasten"}],"ref":"51:14","answerWord":"تَسْتَعْجِلُونَ","answerSound":"audio/72317f2c1bfde3f0a8c2.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"(And it will be said unto them): Taste your torment (which ye inflicted). This is what ye sought to hasten.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"požurivati, tražiti da se ubrza","en":"to hasten, to rush"},"passage":["ذُوقُوا۟","فِتْنَتَكُمْ","هَٰذَا","ٱلَّذِى","كُنتُم","بِهِۦ","تَسْتَعْجِلُونَ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَعْجَلَ"}},{"id":"istajala-13-6-0","words":["verb:istajala"],"options":[{"bs":"i požuruju te","en":"and they ask you to hasten"},{"bs":"požurujete","en":"you (all) hasten"},{"bs":"požurujete me","en":"you (all) ask me to hasten"},{"bs":"požuruju","en":"they hasten"}],"ref":"13:6","answerWord":"وَيَسْتَعْجِلُونَكَ","answerSound":"audio/cbbf6eb4da0e6e94cf51.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And they bid thee hasten on the evil rather than the good, when exemplary punishments have indeed occurred before them. But lo! thy Lord is rich in pardon for mankind despite their wrong, and lo! thy Lord is strong in punishment.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"požurivati, tražiti da se ubrza","en":"to hasten, to rush"},"passage":["وَيَسْتَعْجِلُونَكَ","بِٱلسَّيِّئَةِ","قَبْلَ","ٱلْحَسَنَةِ","وَقَدْ","خَلَتْ","مِن","قَبْلِهِمُ","ٱلْمَثُلَٰتُ","وَإِنَّ","رَبَّكَ","لَذُو","مَغْفِرَةٍ","لِّلنَّاسِ","عَلَىٰ","ظُلْمِهِمْ","وَإِنَّ","رَبَّكَ","لَشَدِيدُ","ٱلْعِقَابِ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَعْجَلَ"}},{"id":"istajala-10-50-9","words":["verb:istajala"],"options":[{"bs":"požuruje","en":"he/it hastens"},{"bs":"i požuruju te","en":"and they ask you to hasten"},{"bs":"požurujete","en":"you (all) hasten"},{"bs":"požurivali ste","en":"you (all) hastened"}],"ref":"10:50","answerWord":"يَسْتَعْجِلُ","answerSound":"audio/a3ae86a9aac27583339b.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say: Have ye thought: When His doom cometh unto you as a raid by night, or in the (busy) day; what is there of it that the guilty ones desire to hasten?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"požurivati, tražiti da se ubrza","en":"to hasten, to rush"},"passage":["قُلْ","أَرَءَيْتُمْ","إِنْ","أَتَىٰكُمْ","عَذَابُهُۥ","بَيَٰتًا","أَوْ","نَهَارًا","مَّاذَا","يَسْتَعْجِلُ","مِنْهُ","ٱلْمُجْرِمُونَ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَعْجَلَ"}},{"id":"istajala-26-204-1","words":["verb:istajala"],"options":[{"bs":"požuruju","en":"they hasten"},{"bs":"požuruju me","en":"they ask me to hasten"},{"bs":"požurujete","en":"you (all) hasten"},{"bs":"i požuruju te","en":"and they ask you to hasten"}],"ref":"26:204","answerWord":"يَسْتَعْجِلُونَ","answerSound":"audio/c11525f29c22cf224924.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Would they (now) hasten on Our doom?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"požurivati, tražiti da se ubrza","en":"to hasten, to rush"},"passage":["أَفَبِعَذَابِنَا","يَسْتَعْجِلُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَعْجَلَ"}},{"id":"istajala-16-1-4","words":["verb:istajala"],"options":[{"bs":"požurujete je","en":"you (all) seek to hasten it"},{"bs":"požuruju te","en":"they urge you to hasten"},{"bs":"požurivali ste","en":"you (all) hastened"},{"bs":"požuruju","en":"they hasten"}],"ref":"16:1","answerWord":"تَسْتَعْجِلُوهُ","answerSound":"audio/0069bd2d588b553a396c.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The commandment of Allah will come to pass, so seek not ye to hasten it. Glorified and Exalted be He above all that they associate (with Him).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"požurivati, tražiti da se ubrza","en":"to hasten, to rush"},"passage":["أَتَىٰٓ","أَمْرُ","ٱللَّهِ","فَلَا","تَسْتَعْجِلُوهُ","سُبْحَٰنَهُۥ","وَتَعَٰلَىٰ","عَمَّا","يُشْرِكُونَ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَعْجَلَ"}},{"id":"istajala-21-37-7","words":["verb:istajala"],"options":[{"bs":"požurujete me","en":"you (all) ask me to hasten"},{"bs":"i požuruju te","en":"and they ask you to hasten"},{"bs":"požuruje","en":"he/it hastens"},{"bs":"požurivali ste","en":"you (all) hastened"}],"ref":"21:37","answerWord":"تَسْتَعْجِلُونِ","answerSound":"audio/a5d3f7a056a58050007d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Man is made of haste. I shall show you My portents, but ask Me not to hasten.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"požurivati, tražiti da se ubrza","en":"to hasten, to rush"},"passage":["خُلِقَ","ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ","مِنْ","عَجَلٍ","سَأُو۟رِيكُمْ","ءَايَٰتِى","فَلَا","تَسْتَعْجِلُونِ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَعْجَلَ"}},{"id":"istajala-29-54-0","words":["verb:istajala"],"options":[{"bs":"požuruju te","en":"they urge you to hasten"},{"bs":"požuruju me","en":"they ask me to hasten"},{"bs":"požurivali ste","en":"you (all) hastened"},{"bs":"požuruje","en":"he/it hastens"}],"ref":"29:54","answerWord":"يَسْتَعْجِلُونَكَ","answerSound":"audio/04990555bdacaa4c048d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They bid thee hasten on the doom, when lo! hell verily will encompass the disbelievers","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"požurivati, tražiti da se ubrza","en":"to hasten, to rush"},"passage":["يَسْتَعْجِلُونَكَ","بِٱلْعَذَابِ","وَإِنَّ","جَهَنَّمَ","لَمُحِيطَةٌۢ","بِٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَعْجَلَ"}},{"id":"istajala-46-24-12","words":["verb:istajala"],"options":[{"bs":"požurivali ste","en":"you (all) hastened"},{"bs":"požuruju","en":"they hasten"},{"bs":"požuruje","en":"he/it hastens"},{"bs":"požuruju te","en":"they urge you to hasten"}],"ref":"46:24","answerWord":"ٱسْتَعْجَلْتُم","answerSound":"audio/b745e208723ebefb497e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then, when they beheld it as a dense cloud coming toward their valleys, they said: Here is a cloud bringing us rain. Nay, but it is that which ye did seek to hasten, a wind wherein is painful torment,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"požurivati, tražiti da se ubrza","en":"to hasten, to rush"},"passage":["فَلَمَّا","رَأَوْهُ","عَارِضًا","مُّسْتَقْبِلَ","أَوْدِيَتِهِمْ","قَالُوا۟","هَٰذَا","عَارِضٌ","مُّمْطِرُنَا","بَلْ","هُوَ","مَا","ٱسْتَعْجَلْتُم","بِهِۦ","رِيحٌ","فِيهَا","عَذَابٌ","أَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[12],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَعْجَلَ"}},{"id":"istajala-51-59-8","words":["verb:istajala"],"options":[{"bs":"požuruju me","en":"they ask me to hasten"},{"bs":"požurujete me","en":"you (all) ask me to hasten"},{"bs":"požurivali ste","en":"you (all) hastened"},{"bs":"požuruju te","en":"they urge you to hasten"}],"ref":"51:59","answerWord":"يَسْتَعْجِلُونِ","answerSound":"audio/a85b1672ab4251ad2ddd.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And lo! for those who (now) do wrong there is an evil day like unto the evil day (which came for) their likes (of old); so let them not ask Me to hasten on (that day).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"požurivati, tražiti da se ubrza","en":"to hasten, to rush"},"passage":["فَإِنَّ","لِلَّذِينَ","ظَلَمُوا۟","ذَنُوبًا","مِّثْلَ","ذَنُوبِ","أَصْحَٰبِهِمْ","فَلَا","يَسْتَعْجِلُونِ"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَعْجَلَ"}},{"id":"saqa-12-41-4","words":["verb:saqa"],"options":[{"bs":"pa napaja","en":"so he/it gives to drink"},{"bs":"napajamo","en":"we give to drink"},{"bs":"i napaja me","en":"and gives me drink"},{"bs":"i napojio ih je","en":"and he/it gave them to drink"}],"ref":"12:41","answerWord":"فَيَسْقِى","answerSound":"audio/800ee85ba126a5481fb5.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"O my two fellow-prisoners! As for one of you, he will pour out wine for his lord to drink; and as for the other, he will be crucified so that the birds will eat from his head. Thus is the case judged concerning which ye did inquire.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"napojiti, zaliti","en":"to give to drink, to water"},"passage":["يَٰصَىٰحِبَىِ","ٱلسِّجْنِ","أَمَّآ","أَحَدُكُمَا","فَيَسْقِى","رَبَّهُۥ","خَمْرًا","وَأَمَّا","ٱلْءَاخَرُ","فَيُصْلَبُ","فَتَأْكُلُ","ٱلطَّيْرُ","مِن","رَّأْسِهِۦ","قُضِىَ","ٱلْأَمْرُ","ٱلَّذِى","فِيهِ","تَسْتَفْتِيَانِ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"سَقَى"}},{"id":"saqa-13-4-12","words":["verb:saqa"],"options":[{"bs":"biva zalijevan","en":"he/it is watered"},{"bs":"i napojeni su","en":"and they were given to drink"},{"bs":"napojio si","en":"you gave to drink"},{"bs":"napajamo","en":"we give to drink"}],"ref":"13:4","answerWord":"يُسْقَىٰ","answerSound":"audio/b6e06d8426039e92da34.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And in the Earth are neighbouring tracts, vineyards and ploughed lands, and date-palms, like and unlike, which are watered with one water. And we have made some of them to excel others in fruit. Lo! herein verily are portents for people who have sense.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"napojiti, zaliti","en":"to give to drink, to water"},"passage":["وَفِى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","قِطَعٌ","مُّتَجَٰوِرَٰتٌ","وَجَنَّٰتٌ","مِّنْ","أَعْنَٰبٍ","وَزَرْعٌ","وَنَخِيلٌ","صِنْوَانٌ","وَغَيْرُ","صِنْوَانٍ","يُسْقَىٰ","بِمَآءٍ","وَٰحِدٍ","وَنُفَضِّلُ","بَعْضَهَا","عَلَىٰ","بَعْضٍ","فِى","ٱلْأُكُلِ","إِنَّ","فِى","ذَٰلِكَ","لَءَايَٰتٍ","لِّقَوْمٍ","يَعْقِلُونَ"],"marked":[12],"facts":{"verb":"سَقَى"}},{"id":"saqa-14-16-3","words":["verb:saqa"],"options":[{"bs":"i biva napojen","en":"and he/it is given to drink"},{"bs":"napojio si","en":"you gave to drink"},{"bs":"i napaja me","en":"and gives me drink"},{"bs":"i napojio ih je","en":"and he/it gave them to drink"}],"ref":"14:16","answerWord":"وَيُسْقَىٰ","answerSound":"audio/c95b0e4f1f3819f49c44.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Hell is before him, and he is made to drink a festering water,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"napojiti, zaliti","en":"to give to drink, to water"},"passage":["مِّن","وَرَآئِهِۦ","جَهَنَّمُ","وَيُسْقَىٰ","مِن","مَّآءٍ","صَدِيدٍ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"سَقَى"}},{"id":"saqa-26-79-3","words":["verb:saqa"],"options":[{"bs":"i napaja me","en":"and gives me drink"},{"bs":"pa je napojio","en":"so he/it gave to drink"},{"bs":"napajamo","en":"we give to drink"},{"bs":"biva zalijevan","en":"he/it is watered"}],"ref":"26:79","answerWord":"وَيَسْقِينِ","answerSound":"audio/b14095c969debd07f5dc.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And Who feedeth me and watereth me.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"napojiti, zaliti","en":"to give to drink, to water"},"passage":["وَٱلَّذِى","هُوَ","يُطْعِمُنِى","وَيَسْقِينِ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"سَقَى"}},{"id":"saqa-28-23-9","words":["verb:saqa"],"options":[{"bs":"napajaju","en":"they give to drink"},{"bs":"i napojeni su","en":"and they were given to drink"},{"bs":"pa napaja","en":"so he/it gives to drink"},{"bs":"i biva napojen","en":"and he/it is given to drink"}],"ref":"28:23","answerWord":"يَسْقُونَ","answerSound":"audio/3dd20b6e2375e28f4c38.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And when he came unto the water of Midian he found there a whole tribe of men, watering. And he found apart from them two women keeping back (their flocks). He said: What aileth you? The two said: We cannot give (our flocks) to drink till the shepherds return from the water; and our father is a very old man.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"napojiti, zaliti","en":"to give to drink, to water"},"passage":["وَلَمَّا","وَرَدَ","مَآءَ","مَدْيَنَ","وَجَدَ","عَلَيْهِ","أُمَّةً","مِّنَ","ٱلنَّاسِ","يَسْقُونَ","وَوَجَدَ","مِن","دُونِهِمُ","ٱمْرَأَتَيْنِ","تَذُودَانِ","قَالَ","مَا","خَطْبُكُمَا","قَالَتَا","لَا","نَسْقِى","حَتَّىٰ","يُصْدِرَ","ٱلرِّعَآءُ","وَأَبُونَا","شَيْخٌ","كَبِيرٌ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"سَقَى"}},{"id":"saqa-28-23-20","words":["verb:saqa"],"options":[{"bs":"napajamo","en":"we give to drink"},{"bs":"i napojeni su","en":"and they were given to drink"},{"bs":"i biva napojen","en":"and he/it is given to drink"},{"bs":"i napojio ih je","en":"and he/it gave them to drink"}],"ref":"28:23","answerWord":"نَسْقِى","answerSound":"audio/670ad4f235462823acbb.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And when he came unto the water of Midian he found there a whole tribe of men, watering. And he found apart from them two women keeping back (their flocks). He said: What aileth you? The two said: We cannot give (our flocks) to drink till the shepherds return from the water; and our father is a very old man.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"napojiti, zaliti","en":"to give to drink, to water"},"passage":["وَلَمَّا","وَرَدَ","مَآءَ","مَدْيَنَ","وَجَدَ","عَلَيْهِ","أُمَّةً","مِّنَ","ٱلنَّاسِ","يَسْقُونَ","وَوَجَدَ","مِن","دُونِهِمُ","ٱمْرَأَتَيْنِ","تَذُودَانِ","قَالَ","مَا","خَطْبُكُمَا","قَالَتَا","لَا","نَسْقِى","حَتَّىٰ","يُصْدِرَ","ٱلرِّعَآءُ","وَأَبُونَا","شَيْخٌ","كَبِيرٌ"],"marked":[20],"facts":{"verb":"سَقَى"}},{"id":"saqa-28-24-0","words":["verb:saqa"],"options":[{"bs":"pa je napojio","en":"so he/it gave to drink"},{"bs":"pa napaja","en":"so he/it gives to drink"},{"bs":"biva zalijevan","en":"he/it is watered"},{"bs":"napajamo","en":"we give to drink"}],"ref":"28:24","answerWord":"فَسَقَىٰ","answerSound":"audio/cf12c163b2914bf602d8.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"So he watered (their flock) for them. Then he turned aside into the shade, and said: My Lord! I am needy of whatever good Thou sendest down for me.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"napojiti, zaliti","en":"to give to drink, to water"},"passage":["فَسَقَىٰ","لَهُمَا","ثُمَّ","تَوَلَّىٰٓ","إِلَى","ٱلظِّلِّ","فَقَالَ","رَبِّ","إِنِّى","لِمَآ","أَنزَلْتَ","إِلَىَّ","مِنْ","خَيْرٍ","فَقِيرٌ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"سَقَى"}},{"id":"saqa-28-25-12","words":["verb:saqa"],"options":[{"bs":"napojio si","en":"you gave to drink"},{"bs":"i napojeni su","en":"and they were given to drink"},{"bs":"pa je napojio","en":"so he/it gave to drink"},{"bs":"pa napaja","en":"so he/it gives to drink"}],"ref":"28:25","answerWord":"سَقَيْتَ","answerSound":"audio/461b40afda85f68849a0.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then there came unto him one of the two women, walking shyly. She said: Lo! my father biddeth thee, that he may reward thee with a payment for that thou didst water (the flock) for us. Then, when he came unto him and told him the (whole) story, he said: Fear not! Thou hast escaped from the wrongdoing folk.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"napojiti, zaliti","en":"to give to drink, to water"},"passage":["فَجَآءَتْهُ","إِحْدَىٰهُمَا","تَمْشِى","عَلَى","ٱسْتِحْيَآءٍ","قَالَتْ","إِنَّ","أَبِى","يَدْعُوكَ","لِيَجْزِيَكَ","أَجْرَ","مَا","سَقَيْتَ","لَنَا","فَلَمَّا","جَآءَهُۥ","وَقَصَّ","عَلَيْهِ","ٱلْقَصَصَ","قَالَ","لَا","تَخَفْ","نَجَوْتَ","مِنَ","ٱلْقَوْمِ","ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ"],"marked":[12],"facts":{"verb":"سَقَى"}},{"id":"saqa-76-21-9","words":["verb:saqa"],"options":[{"bs":"i napojio ih je","en":"and he/it gave them to drink"},{"bs":"pa je napojio","en":"so he/it gave to drink"},{"bs":"i napaja me","en":"and gives me drink"},{"bs":"i biva napojen","en":"and he/it is given to drink"}],"ref":"76:21","answerWord":"وَسَقَىٰهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/9b4e0d54402e4ad2a34d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Their raiment will be fine green silk and gold embroidery. Bracelets of silver will they wear. Their Lord will slake their thirst with a pure drink.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"napojiti, zaliti","en":"to give to drink, to water"},"passage":["عَٰلِيَهُمْ","ثِيَابُ","سُندُسٍ","خُضْرٌ","وَإِسْتَبْرَقٌ","وَحُلُّوٓا۟","أَسَاوِرَ","مِن","فِضَّةٍ","وَسَقَىٰهُمْ","رَبُّهُمْ","شَرَابًا","طَهُورًا"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"سَقَى"}},{"id":"asrafa-17-33-16","words":["verb:asrafa"],"options":[{"bs":"pretjeruje","en":"he/it is excessive"},{"bs":"pretjerujete","en":"you (all) are excessive"},{"bs":"pretjerao je","en":"went to excess"},{"bs":"rasipaju","en":"they are extravagant"}],"ref":"17:33","answerWord":"يُسْرِف","answerSound":"audio/28249308bb30294188f3.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And slay not the life which Allah hath forbidden save with right. Whoso is slain wrongfully, We have given power unto his heir, but let him not commit excess in slaying. Lo! he will be helped.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pretjerati, rasipati","en":"to be excessive, to waste"},"passage":["وَلَا","تَقْتُلُوا۟","ٱلنَّفْسَ","ٱلَّتِى","حَرَّمَ","ٱللَّهُ","إِلَّا","بِٱلْحَقِّ","وَمَن","قُتِلَ","مَظْلُومًا","فَقَدْ","جَعَلْنَا","لِوَلِيِّهِۦ","سُلْطَٰنًا","فَلَا","يُسْرِف","فِّى","ٱلْقَتْلِ","إِنَّهُۥ","كَانَ","مَنصُورًا"],"marked":[16],"facts":{"verb":"أَسْرَفَ"}},{"id":"asrafa-20-127-3","words":["verb:asrafa"],"options":[{"bs":"pretjerao je","en":"went to excess"},{"bs":"pretjeruje","en":"he/it is excessive"},{"bs":"pretjerivali su","en":"they were excessive"},{"bs":"rasipaju","en":"they are extravagant"}],"ref":"20:127","answerWord":"أَسْرَفَ","answerSound":"audio/65b89d81bf2921031451.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Thus do We reward him who is prodigal and believeth not the revelations of his Lord; and verily the doom of the Hereafter will be sterner and more lasting.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pretjerati, rasipati","en":"to be excessive, to waste"},"passage":["وَكَذَٰلِكَ","نَجْزِى","مَنْ","أَسْرَفَ","وَلَمْ","يُؤْمِنۢ","بِـَٔايَٰتِ","رَبِّهِۦ","وَلَعَذَابُ","ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ","أَشَدُّ","وَأَبْقَىٰٓ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"أَسْرَفَ"}},{"id":"asrafa-25-67-4","words":["verb:asrafa"],"options":[{"bs":"rasipaju","en":"they are extravagant"},{"bs":"pretjeruje","en":"he/it is excessive"},{"bs":"pretjerao je","en":"went to excess"},{"bs":"pretjerivali su","en":"they were excessive"}],"ref":"25:67","answerWord":"يُسْرِفُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/6182e9d755441ea5f726.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And those who, when they spend, are neither prodigal nor grudging; and there is ever a firm station between the two;","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pretjerati, rasipati","en":"to be excessive, to waste"},"passage":["وَٱلَّذِينَ","إِذَآ","أَنفَقُوا۟","لَمْ","يُسْرِفُوا۟","وَلَمْ","يَقْتُرُوا۟","وَكَانَ","بَيْنَ","ذَٰلِكَ","قَوَامًا"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"أَسْرَفَ"}},{"id":"asrafa-39-53-3","words":["verb:asrafa"],"options":[{"bs":"pretjerivali su","en":"they were excessive"},{"bs":"pretjeruje","en":"he/it is excessive"},{"bs":"pretjerujete","en":"you (all) are excessive"},{"bs":"rasipaju","en":"they are extravagant"}],"ref":"39:53","answerWord":"أَسْرَفُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/f03eca0d79f5322b3b5c.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say: O My slaves who have been prodigal to their own hurt! Despair not of the mercy of Allah, Who forgiveth all sins. Lo! He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pretjerati, rasipati","en":"to be excessive, to waste"},"passage":["قُلْ","يَٰعِبَادِىَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","أَسْرَفُوا۟","عَلَىٰٓ","أَنفُسِهِمْ","لَا","تَقْنَطُوا۟","مِن","رَّحْمَةِ","ٱللَّهِ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","يَغْفِرُ","ٱلذُّنُوبَ","جَمِيعًا","إِنَّهُۥ","هُوَ","ٱلْغَفُورُ","ٱلرَّحِيمُ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"أَسْرَفَ"}}]